      text: "I'm finding a serious bug in dispatch.ts: on 5xx errors, including a 504 after commit, the code retries with a brand new random reference instead of reusing the original, causing duplicate transfers. This means a lost response gets reported as \"failed\" to the customer even though the money actually moved — and under the intermittent-17 scenario, a third retry compounds this into a duplicate charge.\n\nNext I'm checking authorization.ts and finding there's no approval step at all — the `approvals` table exists but is never used, despite the contract requiring explicit review of amount, source, and destination before any sensitive transfer executes. There's also no check preventing fromAccountId from matching toAccountId, and I need to verify the approvals confirm route in route.ts.\n\nThen in telemetry.ts, I notice `recordEvent` only stores tool and status, dropping arguments, output, error, and operation details — which conflicts with the rule that historical evidence must never be invented, so I need to check whether operator/view.ts is missing data as a result.\n\nLooking at prompt.ts, I see it actually encourages hallucination by telling the model to fill gaps with \"common banking practices\" and give concrete estimates, with no citation requirement and no filtering by validTo or audience — so I want to check search.ts for whether internal docs could leak to customers.\n\nIn run.ts, each call_id gets its own intentId, so a model retry creates a brand new intent; I still need to verify conversation ownership in route.ts, though history slicing to 24 and in-memory locks look fine.\n\nIn client.ts, the timeout is set to 1400ms while the slow-response scenario takes 2.6s, so it times out, gets treated as a 504, and retries with a new reference — another duplicate transfer path. I also note that `response.json()` could throw on non-JSON responses.\n\nNow I'm moving on to review route.ts, operator/view.ts, retrieval, ingestion, the simulator, and the tests.\n\nYa encontré hallazgos graves: en `dispatch.ts` se reintenta con una referencia nueva tras un error 5xx, y en `authorization.ts` falta el paso de aprobación. Sigo revisando la API, el operador, la recuperación de documentos y el simulador.\n\n",
