      title:
        'Looking at the submit function, I notice it never sends an intentId, so each click create…',
      text: 'Looking at the submit function, I notice it never sends an intentId, so each click creates a brand new transfer intent—a double-click or retry after an error would spawn duplicate transfers. There\'s also no confirmation step in the manual transfer form, even though the UI handles a requires_confirmation state, suggesting the design expected an approval flow that the server never actually produces. The amount parsing logic also looks fragile, since it would mishandle something like "1.000,50".\n\nThe operator detail view already renders history, events, bank info, and gaps, but the server returns empty data for all of it—so the frontend is built out while the backend is essentially hollow, meaning the fix is to populate caseDetail. Chat messages are only polled after the conversation finishes, which seems fine.\n\nNow I want to check the fixture files: manifest.json for audience and validTo fields, a handful of FAQ documents that encode business rules (lost response, limits, confirmation, two-accounts, context-guide variants), and seed.ts for conversations and incidents. I\'ll also peek at the conversations.json structure, starting with a jq summary of the manifest and reading through a few of the docs.\n\nLa UI del operador ya muestra historial, eventos y operaciones del banco, pero el servidor devuelve listas vacías. Ahora reviso los documentos del corpus para entender las reglas de negocio que el agente debe respetar.\n\n',
