      text: 'P0.2 complete. Report:\n\n## Commits (after P0.1 `7c51ade`)\n- `08a4ee1` Test: money must not move without an explicit confirmation\n- `031b5c4` Fix: explicit confirmation gate for transfers\n- `9454d47` Expose pending approvals to the agent so later turns can confirm *(extra commit — see deviation)*\n\n## What was implemented\n- **`src/types.ts`**: added `TransferProposal`.\n- **`src/banking/authorization.ts`** (single money gate): ownership check kept; without `approvalId` creates an approval row (10 min TTL), sets intents `awaiting_confirmation`, records `transfer.proposed`, returns `requires_confirmation` with a labeled proposal (`fromLabel`, `toName`/`toLabel` from `/v1/contacts`). With `approvalId`: ordered checks — not found/owner/intent mismatch → "Proposal not found."; payload mismatch → "does not match"; expired → "expired" + intents `expired`; consumed while intent not `unknown` → "already used"; `intents.run_id === ctx.runId` → "Confirmation must come from the customer in a later message." On pass: `consumed_at` set, returns null → dispatch.\n- **`src/agent/tools.ts`**: new `confirm_transfer` tool; `transfer_money` description updated; `list_accounts` now also returns `pendingApprovals` (see deviation).\n- **`src/agent/run.ts`**: added the confirmation instructions verbatim.\n- **`route.ts`**: `confirm_transfer` added to the enum; confirm route left as-is (it already loads approval + intent and calls `transferMoney` with `approvalId` — nothing redundant to remove).\n- **`app/page.tsx`**: proposals panel resolves `fromLabel`/contact name+label from `dashboard.accounts`/`contacts`; `submitTransfer` switches to overview on `requires_confirmation`.\n\n## Tests\n- Before: 14 fail / 13 pass (`evidencias/antes/07-npm-test-antes-approvals.txt`).\n- After: **27 pass / 0 fail** (`evidencias/despues/07-npm-test-despues-approvals.txt`).\n- `npm run typecheck` clean; `npx prettier --check app src tests` clean — note prettier also reformatted `src/retrieval/search.ts` (3-line pre-existing style drift at baseline; included so the check passes).\n- One test interpretation: case (d) calls `authorizeTransfer` directly with altered payload — the real confirm path always sends `approval.payload`, and calling `transferMoney` with altered args trips the pre-existing intents payload guard (409 throw) before reaching the check.\n\n## Live verification (`evidencias/despues/02-...md`)\n- Actions: propose → `requires_confirmation`, 0 ops, balance intact, approval visible in dashboard; confirm → `completed`, −700/+700, 1 op; second confirm → `failed "already used"`, still 1 op.\n- Chat: "Send 5 euros to Bruno for coffee" → *"Please confirm: transfer €5.00 from your Aurora account to Bruno Vidal\'s Horizon account for Coffee. Reply "yes" to authorize it."* (Bruno unchanged, 0 ops). "Yes, confirm" → *"The €5.00 transfer to Bruno Vidal for Coffee is complete. Reference: db91a57e-..."* — Bruno +500 exactly once, intents `completed`.\n- Bank left at `intermittent` seed 17.\n\n## Deviation / surprise (needs your call)\nThe spec\'s chat flow **cannot work as written**: tool outputs aren\'t persisted across turns (only message text is), so in a later message the model has no way to learn the `approvalId` — and re-proposing in the new run creates an intent whose `run_id` equals the confirm\'s `runId`, tripping your own same-run guard. Verified empirically: the model re-proposed and re-asked instead of confirming. Fix (commit `9454d47`): `list_accounts` — which the model already calls each turn — now includes `pendingApprovals` (id + payload), letting it find the original proposal and pass the later-message guard legitimately. Side effect observed: a stale duplicate proposal can remain if the model re-proposes (one expires in 10 min; harmless, but a proposal-dedupe could be a follow-up if you want it).',
