        "Rather than relying on the model to call list_accounts for pending approvals, I'm conside…",
      text: "Rather than relying on the model to call list_accounts for pending approvals, I'm considering a more deterministic design: load pending approvals for the user/conversation in run.ts and inject them directly into the instructions before the loop starts, so the model always sees them regardless of tool calls.\n\nThis also helps with dedup -- since within a short window (say 10 minutes) in the same conversation, an identical unconfirmed proposal with the same payload is almost certainly the same intent, and since it's unconfirmed no money is at risk, I can safely return the existing unconsumed approval instead of creating a duplicate. If dedupe returns an existing approval, the intent's run_id stays as the original, so the confirmation guard still passes correctly. Let me look at the diff now to see how this fits in.\n\n",
