      title:
        "P0 is done, so I'll show Miguel this milestone briefly and move on to P1 (copilot) with t…",
      text: "P0 is done, so I'll show Miguel this milestone briefly and move on to P1 (copilot) with the autonomy I've been granted. Since the sidekick only tested via curl and chat without exercising the UI panel in an actual browser, I'll plan to do a quick Playwright-based browser check myself during P1 verification rather than waiting now.\n\nNow I'm designing P1: the operator copilot with bank reconciliation. First I need to rework the telemetry storage to capture the full data object (arguments, output, error, duration) instead of just tool and status, which should be fine size-wise even for larger outputs like document search results. Then I'm defining a `caseDetail` function that pulls together the incident, customer, conversation history, parsed events, intents with their bank references and statuses, and bank account/operation data fetched as the operator actor -- falling back gracefully to a null/error state if the bank call fails -- plus a reconciliation section to tie everything together.\n\nFor reconciliation I'm matching each intent with a bank_reference against the bank's operations list to determine whether it's completed, not found, or unverified, generating human-readable findings when app and bank records disagree, and noting any gaps where data couldn't be verified. The existing UI already shows history, events, and bank operations, so I just need to add reconciliation findings and a \"Draft reply\" button.\n\nThen I'm sketching the copilot endpoint itself: an operator-only POST route that builds context from the case detail (history, intents, reconciliation, bank ops) plus a document search relevant to the customer's question, then asks the model to return structured JSON with a summary, verified facts, pending checks, discrepancies, a draft reply, and sources -- keeping the implementation simple by requesting JSON output directly rather than overengineering a schema.\n\nI'm validating that JSON with zod, falling back to raw text in draftReply if parsing fails, and writing explicit prompt rules so the model only states facts actually present in the evidence, never claims an unperformed check, separates verified ledger facts from unverified ones, and cites document ids. I decide storing the brief isn't strictly necessary but could log it as a 'copilot.brief' event for traceability -- skipping that for scope. For the reconciliation action itself, when an intent is unknown or failed but the bank shows it completed, the operator can click \"Apply reconciliation\" to update the intent's status, clear the error, and record an 'intent.reconciled' event tied to the operator -- a real state change (not touching the bank) that resolves case-lucia nicely for the demo.\n\nI'm also adding a \"Resolve case\" button that closes an incident, since operators currently have no way to close cases -- a small POST endpoint for that. I'm checking that events and incidents both scope to conversation_id, which they do. For the historic seed data, I'm setting up a failed intent and matching bank operation for lucia under a historic reference so a discrepancy gets detected, and sketching the operator-facing bank call signed by the actor to look up that customer record.\n\nFor the UI, I'm planning a \"Reconciliation\" section in the case detail view showing each intent's app status versus bank status with a badge, plus buttons to apply reconciliation and generate a copilot brief, alongside the close case button. For tests, I'm writing a scenario that seeds the app and bank child, pulls up the case detail for marta's case-lucia, confirms the historic intent shows a discrepancy between completed bank status and failed app status, then verifies reconciling updates the intent to completed.\n\nI'm also checking that case detail throws a 403 for a customer id, that telemetry records tool arguments and outputs like account lists, and noting the brief endpoint can't be unit tested without the live key so I'll verify it manually instead. I'll draft the brief prompt myself since it's product content rather than an eval rubric, and plan to use Playwright MCP to capture before/after screenshots of the operator view, assuming the same tooling is available.\n\nP0 completado: 29 pruebas pasando y confirmado que el dinero solo se mueve una vez por intención, nunca sin confirmación explícita, tanto por API como en chat real. Ahora paso a P1, el copiloto de operador, empezando por cerrar el diseño de datos.\n\n",
