      text: "<subagent_completion_notification>\n[Background subagent with agent_id=sidekick completed]\n\nHardening wave complete. Report:\n\n## Commits\n- `dcfdaa0` Intents: resolve unknown operations against the ledger instead of re-proposing (+ `5c8a92a` type fix)\n- `d8ae6a6` Approvals: confirmation code verified server-side on the customer's own message\n- `d7404f8` Bank client: unreadable response bodies are ambiguous, not rejections (+ `be59522` test type fix)\n- `f098f95` Copilot: untrusted sections, validated sources, no silent fallback, full audit\n- `99740b2` Manual transfers: reset intent after confirmation\n\n## What changed\n- **`src/banking/actions.ts`**: `resolveIntent(userId, intentId)` — unknown+reference → GET ops/:ref → 200 completed / 404 failed / else stays unknown; `transfer.resolved` event. `transferMoney` early-returns: completed → ledger replay (or stored `operationId` if lookup fails); unknown → `resolveIntent` (no re-proposal, no new approval).\n- **`dispatch.ts`**: new UNKNOWN message; reference written via `UPDATE … WHERE bank_reference IS NULL` then re-read (atomic claim, persisted value wins).\n- **`authorization.ts`**: payload dedupe removed; before proposing, identical-payload intents in `unknown`/`processing` are resolved via `resolveIntent` — still unknown → new intent marked `blocked`, returns `{status:'blocked', code:'pending_verification', intentId:<blocking intent>, reference}`. Expiry only applies to `awaiting_confirmation` (unknown+consumed approvals always confirmable). `confirmationCode` exported; `requires_confirmation` includes it; `code` on every failure (`not_found`/`mismatch`/`expired`/`already_used`/`code_required`/`channel_unknown`); `confirmedBy` required — 'message' must contain the code in the run's user message; consume via atomic `UPDATE … AND consumed_at IS NULL`. runId guard removed.\n- **`run.ts`**: resolves unknown intents in the conversation at sendMessage start; remaining unknowns injected as `UNCONFIRMED OPERATIONS`; new confirmation instructions (code required, never re-propose unknown/blocked).\n- **`tools.ts`**: `confirm_transfer` → `confirmedBy:'message'`; `operation_status` resolves a matching unknown intent via `resolveIntent`.\n- **`route.ts`**: dashboard resolves unknowns and returns `pendingOperations`; approvals include `confirmationCode`; confirm route → `confirmedBy:'click'`.\n- **`view.ts`**: `fixable` = bankStatus completed && appStatus !== completed; `closeCase` → 409 while any fixable.\n- **`client.ts`**: unparseable body → `BankError(502)`; transport failure stays 504.\n- **`copilot.ts`**: untrusted `<<<CONVERSATION/DOCUMENTS>>>` markers + audience per doc + instructions verbatim; query = last `user` message (fallback summary); invalid JSON → `HttpError(502)`; `sources` filtered to retrieved ids; single zod schema → `z.toJSONSchema` (stripped `$schema`, `additionalProperties:false`); `copilot.brief` event stores the full brief + sources.\n- **`page.tsx`**: pendingOperations panel (\"Check again\" → refresh); code shown on proposals; brief tagged with `caseId` in state and rendered only for its case (a stale-closure compare wouldn't have worked); brief cleared on reconcile/close; `manualIntentId` reset on confirm (any result) and on `blocked`.\n- **Tests**: +`tests/client.test.ts`; new cases for resolveIntent (ledger resolution, bank-down, replay), expired-approval-over-unknown, blocked-while-unverified, code-required/click/already_used/channel_unknown, closeCase-409. Removed the dedupe tests (i,j), the same-run test (f), and replaced the consumed-proposal test — re-confirming a completed intent now correctly returns the replay.\n\n## Deviations\n- `resolveIntent` is imported in `authorization.ts`/`tools.ts`/`run.ts` via dynamic `await import('../banking/actions')` — `actions` already statically imports `authorization`, and a static back-import would be a module cycle.\n- The unverified scan runs **before** the bank ownership call in the no-approvalId branch — required so the blocked path works with the bank down; ownership is still checked before any proposal or dispatch.\n- One `git commit --amend` slipped in for the B1 type fix (my own commit, local only) — can't undo safely; flagged.\n- Live, `pendingOperations` was already `[]` on the first dashboard read — the dashboard resolves unknowns itself, which *is* the verification.\n\n## Verification — **44 pass / 0 fail** (`evidencias/despues/10-npm-test-hardening.txt`), typecheck + prettier clean.\n- read-unavailable: confirm → `unknown`; `GET /api/dashboard` → resolved to `completed`, `transfer.resolved` event, **1 bank operation**.\n- Chat: \"Send 5 euros to Bruno for coffee\" → *\"…Responde con el código: **FFD800**.\"*; \"yes\" → *\"No se pudo completar: el banco solicita el código de confirmación…\"* (0 ops, Bruno unchanged); \"confirm FFD800\" → *\"La transferencia se completó: 5,00 € a Bruno… Referencia: fe171474…\"* (1 op, +500 once). Full texts in `evidencias/despues/11-confirmacion-por-codigo.md`.\n- State left: `intent-historic-lucia` still `failed`, 0 events in `conv-lucia-support`, case-lucia open; bank at `intermittent` 17. Residue: `verify-unknown-2` awaiting_confirmation (self-expires), and the completed coffee transfer in conv `d9f94463`.\n</subagent_completion_notification>",
