        'It looks like the second proposal confirmation is consuming a second operation because th…',
      text: "It looks like the second proposal confirmation is consuming a second operation because the first proposal resolves to 'completed' after being marked 'unknown' due to a read failure. The scenario only fails the *first* read, so the subsequent POST request for the second proposal succeeds. For test (b), the 'Alquiler' concept blocking is already covered by an existing test, so I'll modify that test to use a different concept string for the second proposal to meet the spec.\n\nI'm re-evaluating the test order for proposal processing. Test (c) has two sub-cases: one that fails immediately and one that fails due to staleness. The stale case requires the bank service, but test (b) kills the bank. Therefore, I need to run tests that require the bank first, placing the bank-killing test last. Test (a)'s confirmation logic seems correct, handling the unresolvedEquivalent case after the initial checks.",
