      text: "I'm updating the `operation_status` tool. Previously, it only checked for 'unknown' intents, but now it also checks for 'processing' intents. This should allow `resolveIntent` to correctly complete operations that are still pending. I'm also passing the `operation` object directly to `resolveIntent` when the intent is pending, which seems more logical than just passing the `id`.\n\nI'm refining the error handling for `bankRequest`. If it throws a `BankError` with a 404 status and there's a pending intent, I'll resolve that intent and set it as the result. Other errors will be rethrown and caught by the outer handler, marking the operation as failed. When an intent is pending, the result should include the resolved intent's status, so I'll merge `resolved.status` into the result.\n\nI need to fetch the full payload for completed or failed intents, not just the ID, so I'll update the initial query to select `id`, `payload`, and `bank_reference`. I also need to add an \"OPERATIONS RESOLVED\" block after the \"UNCONFIRMED\" block. Additionally, I'll filter out 'copilot.brief' events from `AGENT ACTIVITY` by updating the `detail.events` filter in `copilot.ts`. Finally, I'm adding a test case to `operator.test.ts` to ensure that running `operation_status` on an unknown intent reference correctly results in a 'completed' status for the intent, even when the bank operation is completed. This requires seeding the test context with an unknown intent and its corresponding bank operation.",
