        'Wave 2 complete. Report: ## Commits - `4c093ff` Approvals: the confirming message must be…',
      text: 'Wave 2 complete. Report:\n\n## Commits\n- `4c093ff` Approvals: the confirming message must be the code and nothing else\n- `b5f9ad1` Transfers: block equivalent operations while one is unresolved, at proposal and at confirmation\n- `d7be760` Approvals: expiry is terminal; one active proposal per intent\n- `8ea8fac` Bank client: keep the HTTP status when the body is unreadable\n- `87993a6` Agent and copilot: single-lookup resolution, resolved operations in context, trusted sections tightened\n- `57b9715` UI: drop the manual intent id once its proposal is gone\n\n## What changed\n- **`authorization.ts`**: message confirmations now normalize the run\'s user message (lowercase, non-alnum→space, collapse), extract the code as one or more consecutive tokens (covers `confirm abc-123`), and require every remaining word to be in the affirmative allowlist — `no`, `example`, etc. → `code_required`. Expiry is terminal: expired approval + non-unknown intent → always `expired` fail (intent only marked `expired` from `awaiting_confirmation`). One active approval per intent: re-proposing returns the existing approvalId/code/expiresAt. Before consuming, `unresolvedEquivalent` blocks with `pending_verification` (no consume, no status change).\n- **`resolve.ts`**: `resolveIntent` now covers `processing` (no reference → `processing`; 404 → `failed` only if unknown or older than 5 min) and accepts an optional pre-fetched `operation`. New `unresolvedEquivalent(userId, input, excludeId)` — equivalence = from/to/amount (concept ignored).\n- **`tools.ts`**: `operation_status` does one bank lookup; 200 + pending intent → `resolveIntent(..., operation)`; 404 + pending → normal `resolveIntent` (→ failed); result carries `intentStatus`.\n- **`run.ts`**: turn-start resolutions captured; completed/failed ones injected as `OPERATIONS RESOLVED SINCE THE LAST MESSAGE`. Prompt wording updated (only-the-code + negation warning; pending-proposals line reworded).\n- **`client.ts`**: unreadable body on error status → `BankError(response.status, \'…(unreadable body).\')`; ok status → 502.\n- **`copilot.ts`**: `copilot.brief` events excluded from AGENT ACTIVITY; INSTRUCTIONS gained the customer-provided-fields clause.\n- **`page.tsx`**: `refresh()` clears `manualIntentId` when no active approval references it (covers chat-confirmed proposals).\n\n## Tests — **51 pass / 0 fail** (`evidencias/despues/12-npm-test-hardening-2.txt`), typecheck + prettier clean.\nNew coverage: negation/mention-with-code → code_required + unconsumed; bare/split code → completed; double-expired-confirm; re-propose same intent; A/B block-until-resolution (2 legit ops); processing blocks; stale processing → failed → proposal allowed; operation_status single-lookup; unreadable 404 body.\n\n## Live chat (`evidencias/despues/13-negacion-con-codigo.md`)\n- "Send 5 euros to Bruno for coffee" → *"Please confirm this transfer by replying **confirm 2A4842**…"*\n- "no, don\'t do it, the code 2A4842 was just an example" → *"Understood—I won\'t make the transfer."* — **0 ops, approval unconsumed, intent awaiting_confirmation** (server would have failed `code_required`; the model accepted the cancellation, which the spec allows).\n- "confirm 2A4842" → *"The €5.00 transfer to Bruno for Coffee was completed. Reference: 9c7e3d80…"* — Bruno +500 exactly once.\n\n## Deviations\n- The spec\'s test (a) needs A to remain unknown during B\'s confirm — under `read-unavailable` the bank\'s single armed read failure is already consumed, so the test re-arms it via `bankDb` (`UPDATE scenario SET read_failures=1`) before confirming B. With a live bank, resolving A on the spot and letting B proceed is the designed behavior.\n- `resolveIntent`\'s optional `operation` param landed in the B2 commit (same-file rewrite) instead of B5.\n- State: `intent-historic-lucia` untouched (`failed`, 0 events, case open); bank at `intermittent` 17.',
