      text: "The code-matching logic checks edge cases around prefix matching correctly, so the hardening looks solid. Now I should update the todo list and move on to deciding priority P3, keeping in mind it's Saturday afternoon with limited time remaining.\n\nThe mandatory items remaining are README updates, the submission README, a production build test, a reset/fresh-run test, sessions export, the video, and the final ZIP. P3's refactor is optional and risky given the size of page.tsx and the CSS tokens work, and Miguel's preference for finishing things fully rather than halfway makes me want to skip it unless time remains after the core deliverables and video are done.\n\nI should give Miguel a milestone update now since he asked to be kept informed, then move into writing docs — starting with the submission README myself, pulling together test counts, file changes, and commit history. I also need to decide where the evidence files live, planning to move `evidencias/` into the submission folder at packaging time and reference those paths in the README.\n\nEndurecimiento 2 aprobado (51 tests): duplicados por respuesta perdida arreglados, confirmación por código de 6 caracteres verificado en servidor, estado `unknown` honesto, copiloto de operador con reconciliación app↔banco y revisiones de Codex/Grok resueltas. Dejo el refactor P3 para el final solo si sobra tiempo, y paso ahora al cierre: documentación, build de producción, reset y arranque limpio, exports de sesiones, vídeo y ZIP.\n\n",
