      text: "Output from command in shell 7dcdab:\n\u001b[90mCapture key frames from a composition as PNG screenshots for visual verification (hyperframes snapshot v0.8.145)\u001b[39m\n\n\u001b[4m\u001b[1mUSAGE\u001b[22m\u001b[24m \u001b[36mhyperframes snapshot [OPTIONS] [DIR]\u001b[39m\n\n\u001b[4m\u001b[1mARGUMENTS\u001b[22m\u001b[24m\n\n  \u001b[36mDIR\u001b[39m    Project directory\n\n\u001b[4m\u001b[1mOPTIONS\u001b[22m\u001b[24m\n\n      \u001b[36m-o, --output=<output>\u001b[39m    Directory to write snapshots into (default: <project>/snapshots)                                                                                                                                                                                                                           \n          \u001b[36m--frames=<frames>\u001b[39m    Number of evenly-spaced frames to capture (default: 5) \u001b[90m(Default: 5)\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                              \n                  \u001b[36m--at=<at>\u001b[39m    Comma-separated timestamps in seconds (e.g., --at 3.0,10.5,18.0). Each is captured at that exact instant, not snapped to a frame.                                                                                                                                                          \n        \u001b[36m--timeout=<timeout>\u001b[39m    Ms to wait for runtime to initialize (default: 5000) \u001b[90m(Default: 5000)\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                             \n            \u001b[36m--angle=<angle>\u001b[39m    Orthogonal 3D camera for depth/occlusion checks: a preset (front|iso|top|side) or 'yaw,pitch' degrees. Tilts the whole stage before screenshotting (real pixels, not bbox markers).                                                                                                        \n                      \u001b[36m--end\u001b[39m    Always include a readable end-of-timeline frame (default: true). Pass --no-end to capture only your exact --at times. \u001b[90m(Default: true)\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                            \n                   \u001b[36m--no-end\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               \n              \u001b[36m--zoom=<zoom>\u001b[39m    Zoom into a CSS selector or an exact pixel region 'x,y,w,h'. Crops a high-density screenshot instead of the full frame — a raised deviceScaleFactor, never CSS zoom or viewport resizing, so layout stays identical. A selector matching nothing is an error, not a silent full-frame shot.\n  \u001b[36m--zoom-scale=<zoom_scale>\u001b[39m    Device-scale-factor density for --zoom crops (default: 3) \u001b[90m(Default: 3)\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                           \n        \u001b[36m--against=<against>\u001b[39m    Reference video (e.g. footage being rebuilt): also save its frame at each captured time and a render|reference pair sheet                                                                                                                                                                  \n      \u001b[36m--describe=<describe>\u001b[39m    Gemini vision frame analysis. Runs by default when GEMINI_API_KEY is set. Pass a custom question (e.g. --describe 'Is the logo visible in every beat?') to override the default prompt, or --describe false to opt out.                                                                    \n                    \u001b[36m--proxy\u001b[39m    Auto-transcode browser-hostile video codecs for snapshots (default: on; overrides hyperframes.json media.autoProxy)                                                                                                                                                                        \n              \u001b[36m--browser-gpu\u001b[39m    Use hardware browser GPU capture; pass --no-browser-gpu for deterministic SwiftShader (default: auto-detect, PRODUCER_BROWSER_GPU_MODE overrides)                                                                                                                                          \n\n\n\nExit code: 0",
