      text: "It seems `git stash pop` restored the monolithic `app/globals.css` file, overwriting my version that used `@import` statements. My subsequent Python scripts modified the split files in `app/styles/` but didn't affect `globals.css`, leaving the styles orphaned. The parity check showing 0px difference was misleading because it was comparing the old, monolithic CSS.\n\nI'm confused about the state of `globals.css`. The `git stash pop` command likely restored the `@import` version, and my scripts only modified `app/styles/`. However, `git status` at commit time didn't show `globals.css` as modified, implying it was already the monolithic version. This suggests either the stash pop failed or a later command reverted the file.\n\nI'm realizing that `git stash -- app/globals.css app/styles` only stashed changes to `globals.css`, not the untracked `app/styles`. If `globals.css` was then overwritten with the HEAD version, and the stash pop silently failed, the subsequent parity tests would have been comparing the monolithic CSS. This means the \"0px bisect\" results are invalid, and only the initial size mismatch was a true test. I need to check the stash list and the current `globals.css` content to confirm this and then fix the file.",
