      text: "I've found that hoisting groups E, F, and G broke the layout on pages with footers, causing pixel differences even though element sizes are now equal. It seems to be related to `.subtle-tag` and `.muted`/`.case-empty` classes, as the `documents` pages are fine while others like `marta-cases` show discrepancies. I'm investigating if the order of these elements or their specific content is the cause.\n\nI'm seeing some CSS specificity issues. Hoisting `.subtle-tag` from 760 to ~230 means selectors between 231-759 could override it, but `.section-title > span` at 548 comes after the hoisted rule, and its specificity is higher anyway. For `.muted` (1072→~240), selectors between 240-1071 could override it, but the base `p` rule still wins. `.case-empty` (1076→~245) has similar name conflicts with `.chat-empty`.\n\nI'm seeing conflicts with `@keyframes spin` and another animation, `pulse`, at 905. It seems the `footer` element, now hoisted earlier, might be interfering with `.alert`, `.error`, and `.notice` styles, causing a large pixel difference (13075px) on `marta-case-lucia`. I'll test E group in isolation to confirm if the footer and alerts are the primary cause.",
