      text: "I'm seeing a specificity conflict with `.case-empty h2` and `.case-detail h2`. The `font-size` is being overridden from 21px to 25px because the rule in `operator.css` is now loaded after the one in `base.css`, and they have equal specificity. This also seems to be happening with `.case-empty p`. I need to investigate the diffs in `case-lucia` and `.finding` to see if similar hoisting issues are at play there.\n\nI'm checking the diff for `marta-case-lucia` and suspect `.status-pill` or `.case-detail h2` might be involved, as the latter is 25px in the reference. However, the `case-empty h2` rule doesn't apply here. The elements around y815, like `.reconciliation-row` and `.finding`, aren't hoisted, but `.primary-button` is. I'm still trying to pinpoint the exact element causing the issue in the diff.\n\nI'm considering a practical approach to fix specificity conflicts like `.case-empty h2`. Instead of hoisting `.case-empty*`, I could either consolidate it or keep it in its original position within `operator.css`. Keeping it there is semantically off but safe, as other CSS files are global. A cleaner fix is to revert the hoisting of `.case-empty` and `.muted` rules, moving them back to their original position in `operator.css` to resolve the `font-size` issue.\n\nI'm re-evaluating the `marta-case-lucia` diff, specifically around y815-1003. The `.case-empty` rule doesn't apply here, so the issue isn't with `case-empty h2` or `p`. I'm checking computed styles for `h3` in `.case-detail` and found the competitor's `h3` is 15px, while ours is 12px. The order of rules (`h3` base vs. `.case-detail h3`) seems fine. I'll proceed with un-hoisting `.muted` and `.case-empty` back to their original position in `operator.css` and re-running to see if the diff resolves. I'll also check `.subtle-tag` hoisting, which appears unaffected.",
